From 56dfa8e46910496f7d7bbbd480f6cb707f017307 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:55:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(app): refuse a drill hole deeper than the flute from
 the stock surface, prove the holder clear

Every drilling op now refuses by name a hole whose depth from the stock
surface exceeds the tool's usable flute length - past the flutes the
shank feeds into uncut stock, a collision. Cross holes are measured from
the mouths cross_stock moved out to the raw surface (#77); axial holes
from the highest material (part, plus the setup stock clipped to the R
plane) over the drill's disk down to each cycle's bottom.

The holder (holder_d / holder_len, its face flute_len + shank_len behind
the tip) is proven clear of the stock: axially, its face stays above the
material over its disk; on the cross drill, on every move, either its
lower edge rides above the stock's Z top or its swept footprint stays
outside the stock radius - so a holder that would sweep the end face on
the opposite-station swing is refused by name (the swing is not raised).

New logic lives in operation/drill_reach.rs. Fixtures that drilled past
a 12 mm jobber flute (real reach collisions under the rule) take a
long-series flute; the M1.6 deep-hole "warns and still generates" test
becomes "is refused by name", and posting's warned-path test moves to a
shank-hit contour.

Fixes #84

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
