From d8a9d4d240b768849a4cab2503c2073cf019a21e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:27:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(app): drill reach review fixes - bore/tap shank fit,
 per-Z-band holder, wider-body cross reach

Review findings on PR #90:
- Tap, Bore and BackBore run in an existing hole: no longer held to the
  flute; past the flute the shank must fit the hole's diameter (refused
  by name otherwise), the holder law kept.
- The cross holder is judged per Z band: each move's holder Z extent
  against the widest part/stock radius inside that band (facets clipped
  to it), replacing the global stock radius and Z-top skip - a far
  flange on a stepped shaft no longer refuses a hole in a slim section.
- An off-centre cross hole's reach is measured from where the wider of
  drill and shank meets the raw bar (to_raw_mouths returns the extra);
  the mouth stays at the drill's edge.
- A non-finite or negative holder_d/holder_len is refused by name, not
  read as "no holder"; 0 still means no holder.
- meets_disk skips facets with no 3D area and reads walls by their
  edges only; drill_reach unit tests move to drill_reach_tests.rs.
- cross_support / RECOMMENDED.md: the raw box face depth is 38 mm (47
  is the corner radius, #85); review-fixes note on the #84 entry.

Tests: drill_reach (+2), new drill_reach_fit (3), drill_reach unit (+3).

Refs #84

